logs prints the daemon's log file (where it reports the radios it found,
what it is doing and why something failed). -f keeps printing as it grows.

Usage:
  ley daemon logs [flags]

Examples:
  ley daemon logs          # the whole log so far
  ley daemon logs -f       # follow it while you try something

Flags:
  -f, --follow   keep printing as the log grows
  -h, --help     help for logs

Global Flags:
      --ascii           draw with ASCII only (no box, bar or tree glyphs)
      --bin string      path to the leylined binary
      --color string    colour output: auto, always or never (default "auto")
      --json            machine output: proto3 JSON (NDJSON for streams)
      --log string      daemon log file (default: ~/Library/Logs/Leyline/leylined.log)
      --socket string   daemon socket path (default: user daemon UDS, $LEYLINE_SOCKET)
